bgg -- the ith differential of the complex R(M)
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        bgg(i,M,E)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the cohomological index
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, graded S-module
      * E, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, exterior
        algebra
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix representing the ith
        differential

Description
===========

This function takes as input an integer i and a finitely generated graded
S-module M, and returns the ith map in R(M), which is an adjoint of the
multiplication map between M_i and M_{i+1}.
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/32003[x_0..x_2];                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = ZZ/32003[e_0..e_2, SkewCommutative=>true];|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = coker matrix {{x_0^2, x_1^2, x_2^2}};     |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : bgg(1,M,E)                                    |
|                                                   |
|o4 = {-2} | e_1 e_0 0   |                          |
|     {-2} | e_2 0   e_0 |                          |
|     {-2} | 0   e_2 e_1 |                          |
|                                                   |
|             3      3                              |
|o4 : Matrix E  <-- E                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : bgg(2,M,E)                                    |
|                                                   |
|o5 = {-3} | e_2 e_1 e_0 |                          |
|                                                   |
|             1      3                              |
|o5 : Matrix E  <-- E                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+

