tateResolution -- finite piece of the Tate resolution
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        tateResolution(m,E,l,h)
  * Inputs:
      * m, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a presentation matrix for a
        module
      * E, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, exterior
        algebra
      * l, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, lower cohomological degree
      * h, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, upper bound on the
        cohomological degree
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a finite piece of the Tate
        resolution

Description
===========

This function takes as input a presentation matrix m of a finitely generated
graded S-module M an exterior algebra E and two integers l and h. If r is the
regularity of M, then this function computes the piece of the Tate resolution
from cohomological degree l to cohomological degree max(r+2,h). For instance,
for the homogeneous coordinate ring of a point in the projective plane:
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/32003[x_0..x_2];                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : E = ZZ/32003[e_0..e_2, SkewCommutative=>true];|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : m = matrix{{x_0,x_1}};                        |
|                                                   |
|             1      2                              |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : regularity coker m                            |
|                                                   |
|o4 = 0                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T = tateResolution(m,E,-2,4)                  |
|                                                   |
|      1      1      1      1      1      1      1  |
|o5 = E  <-- E  <-- E  <-- E  <-- E  <-- E  <-- E   |
|                                                   |
|     0      1      2      3      4      5      6   |
|                                                   |
|o5 : Complex                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : betti T                                       |
|                                                   |
|            0 1 2 3 4 5 6                          |
|o6 = total: 1 1 1 1 1 1 1                          |
|        -4: 1 1 1 1 1 1 1                          |
|                                                   |
|o6 : BettiTally                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : T.dd_1                                        |
|                                                   |
|o7 = {-4} | e_2 |                                  |
|                                                   |
|             1      1                              |
|o7 : Matrix E  <-- E                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note symExt: symExt, -- the first differential of the complex R(M)

